i><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-math-sin-function">SIN()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-math-sinh-function">SINH()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-math-sqrt-function">SQRT()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-math-sum-function">SUM()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-math-tan-function">TAN()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-math-tanh-function">TANH()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-math-trunc-function">TRUNC()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-math-abs-function">abs()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-math-acos-function">acos()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-math-asin-function">asin()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-math-atan2-function">atan2()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-math-atan-function">atan()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-math-avg-function">avg()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-math-bitand-function">bitand()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-math-ceil-function">ceil()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-math-cos-function">cos()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-math-cosh-function">cosh()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-math-count-function">count()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-math-exp-function">exp()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-math-floor-functions">floor()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-math-greatest-function">greatest()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-math-least-function">least()</a></li></ul></div></div></div><div class="accordion-item" style="background-color:var(--sidebar)"><h2 class="accordion-header" id="flush-heading11"><button aria-controls="flush-collapse11" aria-expanded="true" class="accordion-button sidebar-btn" data-bs-target="#flush-collapse11" data-bs-toggle="collapse" type="button">Oracle String Function</button></h2><div aria-labelledby="flush-heading11" class="accordion-collapse collapse show" id="flush-collapse11"><div class="accordion-body"><ul><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-string">Oracle String</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-string-ascii-function">ASCII</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-string-asciistr-function">ASCIISTR</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-string-chr-function">CHR</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-string-compose-function">COMPOSE</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-string-concat-function">CONCAT</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-string-concat-with-function">CONCAT WITH ||</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-string-convert-function">CONVERT</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-string-decompose-function">DECOMPOSE</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-string-dump-function">DUMP</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-string-instr4-function">INSTR4()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-string-instrb-function">INSTRB()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-string-instrc-function">INSTRC()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-string-length2-function">LENGTH2()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-string-length4-function">LENGTH4()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-string-lengthb-function">LENGTHB()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-string-lengthc-function">LENGTHC()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-string-length-function">LENGTH()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-string-lower-function">LOWER()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-string-lpad-function">LPAD()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-string-ltrim-function">LTRIM()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-string-nchr-function">NCHR()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-string-regexp_instr-function">REGEXP_INSTR()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-string-regexp_replace-function">REGEXP_REPLACE()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-string-regexp_substr-function">REGEXP_SUBSTR()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-string-replace-function">REPLACE()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-string-rpad-function">RPAD()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-string-rtrim-function">RTRIM()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-string-soundex-function">SOUNDEX()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-string-substr-function">SUBSTR()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-string-translate-function">TRANSLATE()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-string-trim-function">TRIM()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-string-upper-function">UPPER()</a></li><li class="leftmenu"><a href="/oracle-string-vsize-function">Oracle VSIZE() Function</a></li></ul></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="col-12 col-md-7"><div class="overview"><div id="city"><table><tbody><tr><td><div id="bottomnextup"><a class="next" href="what-is-oracle">next →</a></div><h1 class="h1">Oracle Tutorial</h1><div style="font-size:14px;margin-top:5px;margin-bottom:5px;color:#6f6e6e"><span>30 Jul 2025</span> | <span><i aria-hidden="true" class="fa fa-clock-o"></i> 3 min read</span></div><p>Oracle tutorial provides basic and advanced concepts of Oracle. Our Oracle tutorial is designed for beginners and professionals.</p><p>Oracle is a <a href="what-is-rdbms">relational database management system</a>. It is widely used in enterprise applications.</p><p>Our Oracle tutorial includes all topics of <a href="oracle-database-architecture">Oracle database</a> such as insert record, update record, delete record, select record, create table, drop table etc. There are also given Oracle interview questions to help you better understand the Oracle database.</p><h2 class="h2">Oracle Tools and Utilities</h2><p>List of some tools and utilities available in oracle are:</p><h3 class="h3">1. Application Development Tools</h3><p>List of following tools are used for the application development.</p><ul class="points"><li><strong>SQL Plus:</strong> It is used to control tables and other database objects in an Oracle's database.</li><li><strong>Developer/2000:</strong> It is a collection of tools which supports the development of client/server applications. It includes:</li><li><strong>Oracle Forms:</strong> This is an enterprise tool used to create data entry forms and menus.</li><li><strong>Oracle Reports:</strong> This is a report authoring tool used to create reports that access tables in Oracle databases.</li><li><strong>Oracle's Graphics:</strong> It is used to create charts and presentation graphics from database queries.</li><li><strong>Designer/2000:</strong> It is a collection of tools that supports the development of complex applications that may span multiple organizations within an enterprise.</li><li><strong>Programmer/2000:</strong> It includes the pre compilers such as libraries routines and utilities that can be linked with programming languages such as C, C++, Java and some other host language to allow access to Oracle's databases.</li></ul><h3 class="h3">2. Database Utilities</h3><p>List of following tools are used for the database utilities.</p><ul class="points"><li><strong>Enterprise Manager:</strong> It is collection of utilities for managing Oracle databases.</li><li><strong>Export and Import: </strong>It allows a user to export data from an Oracle database into a machine readable file or to import data from a machine readable file.</li><li><strong>SQL Loader:</strong> It is used to load ASCII data files into an Oracle database.</li></ul><h3 class="h3">3. Middleware and Connectivity Products</h3><p>List of following tools are used for the middleware and connectivity products.</p><ul class="points"><li><strong>SQL NET:</strong> This allows an Oracle tool running on a client machine to access data on a separate server machine.</li><li><strong>Oracle ODBC drivers:</strong> This driver is used for connecting software's such as Visual Basic to Oracle databases using the ODBC standard.</li></ul><h2 class="h2">Uses of Oracle</h2><p>Here is a list of some of the uses of Oracle:</p><ul class="points"><li>It is used in online transaction processing such as banking, finance, e-commerce, trading, etc.</li><li>It is used in data warehousing to archive historical data.</li></ul><hr/><h2 class="h2 center textshadow">Oracle Index</h2><hr/><div class="responsivediv"><div class="col-3"><p><strong>Oracle Tutorial</strong></p><ul class="points"><li><a href="oracle-tutorial">Oracle Tutorial</a></li><li><a href="what-is-oracle">What is Oracle</a></li></ul><p><strong>Oracle Tables</strong></p><ul class="points"><li><a href="oracle-create-table">Create Table</a></li><li><a href="oracle-create-table-as">Create Table As</a></li><li><a href="oracle-alter-table">Alter Table</a></li><li><a href="oracle-drop-table">Drop Table</a></li><li><a href="oracle-global-temp-tables">Global Temp Tables</a></li><li><a href="oracle-local-temp-tables">Local Temp Tables</a></li></ul><p><strong>Oracle Views</strong></p><ul class="points"><li><a href="oracle-view">Create View</a></li></ul><p><strong>Oracle Query</strong></p><ul class="points"><li><a href="oracle-queries">Oracle Queries</a></li><li><a href="oracle-select">Oracle Select</a></li><li><a href="oracle-insert">Oracle Insert</a></li><li><a href="oracle-insert-all">Oracle Insert All</a></li><li><a href="oracle-update">Oracle Update</a></li><li><a href="oracle-delete">Oracle Delete</a></li><li><a href="oracle-truncate-table">Truncate Table</a></li></ul></div><div class="col-3"><p><strong>Oracle Clauses</strong></p><ul class="points"><li><a href="oracle-distinct-clause">Oracle DISTINCT</a></li><li><a href="oracle-from-clause">Oracle FROM</a></li><li><a href="oracle-order-by-clause">Oracle ORDER BY</a></li><li><a href="oracle-group-by-clause">Oracle GROUP BY</a></li><li><a href="oracle-having-clause">Oracle HAVING</a></li></ul><p><strong>Oracle Operators</strong></p><ul class="points"><li><a href="oracle-union">Oracle Union</a></li><li><a href="oracle-union-all">Oracle Union All</a></li><li><a href="oracle-intersect">Oracle Intersect</a></li><li><a href="oracle-minus">Oracle Minus</a></li></ul><p><strong>Oracle Joins</strong></p><ul class="points"><li><a href="oracle-joins">Oracle Joins</a></li><li><a href="oracle-inner-join">Inner Join</a></li><li><a href="oracle-outer-join">Outer Join</a></li><li><a href="oracle-equi-join">Equi Join</a></li><li><a href="oracle-self-join">Self Join</a></li><li><a href="oracle-cross-join">Cross Join</a></li><li><a href="oracle-anti-join">Anti Join</a></li><li><a href="oracle-semi-join">Semi Join</a></li></ul></div><div class="col-3"><p><strong>Oracle Advance</strong></p><ul class="points"><li><a href="oracle-procedure">Oracle Procedure</a></li><li><a href="oracle-function">Oracle Function</a></li><li><a href="oracle-cursor">Oracle Cursor</a></li><li><a href="oracle-trigger">Oracle Trigger</a></li><li><a href="oracle-before-trigger">Oracle BEFORE Trigger</a></li><li><a href="oracle-after-trigger">Oracle AFTER Trigger</a></li><li><a href="oracle-drop-trigger">Oracle DROP Trigger</a></li><li><a href="oracle-disable-trigger">Oracle DISABLE Trigger</a></li><li><a href="oracle-enable-trigger">Oracle ENABLE Trigger</a></li></ul><p><strong>Interview Questions</strong></p><ul class="points"><li><a href="oracle-interview-questions">Oracle Interview</a></li><li><a href="sql-interview-questions">SQL Interview</a></li><li><a href="pl-sql-interview-questions">PL/SQL Interview</a></li><li><a href="mongodb-interview-questions">MongoDB Interview</a></li></ul></div></div><hr/><h2 class="h2">Prerequisite</h2><p>Before learning Oracle, you must have the basic knowledge of computer fundamentals.</p><h2 class="h2">Audience</h2><p>Our Oracle tutorial is designed to help beginners and professionals.</p><h2 class="h2">Problem</h2><p>We assure that you will not find any problem in this Oracle t